  "views": {
    "hero": "three_quarter",
    "reads": {
      "front": "From behind the caster: the warning circle lies ahead on the ground, the meteor drops in from high on the far side, growing as it nears with its fire trail streaming up behind it, and the impact fills the frame with a fireball, flying rock and a dust wave rolling toward the camera.",
      "side": "The best read of the fall: a diagonal streak from the top of the frame down to the target, white-hot at the rock and cooling to red flame and then grey smoke along the trail; the fireball and the smoke column rise tall over a flat shockwave.",
      "top": "The ground story carries it: the warning circle grows and pulses, the meteor shows as a short streak sliding in onto the centre, then a ring of flash, the shockwave and the dust wave expand evenly in every direction, debris scatters outward and the crater with glowing cracks is left.",
      "three_quarter": "Hero view. The circle reads as an ellipse on the ground, the meteor comes down at an angle with the trail hanging in the air behind it, the fireball and smoke column have height, and the debris lands all around the crater."
    }
  },
